# UI Conventions

## Color System — Single Source of Truth

All colors live in `frontend/src/app/globals.css` as CSS custom properties.
**Never write hex, rgba, or named colors in component files, `constants.ts`, or anywhere else.**

### Token Reference

| Token | Value | Use |
| ----- | ----- | --- |
| `--color-primary` | `#2F2FE4` | Brand, buttons, active states |
| `--color-primary-hover` | `#5151e3` | Button hover |
| `--color-primary-light` | `#c2c2ff` | Light accent |
| `--color-secondary` | `#1f1f1f` | Dark text, Three.js dark geometry |
| `--color-secondary-hover` | `#787878` | Muted text |
| `--color-secondary-light` | `#dbdbdb` | Borders, dividers |
| `--color-secondary-lighter` | `#f3f3f3` | Backgrounds |
| `--color-success` | `#10B981` | |
| `--color-error` | `#EF4444` | |
| `--color-warning` | `#F59E0B` | |
| `--color-info` | `#3B82F6` | |
| `--color-material-start/mid/end` | `#67bfb4` / `#ffbf6d` / `#eb5c52` | Acoustic absorption gradient |
| `--color-receiver` | `#f0a938` | Three.js receiver cube |
| `--color-overlay-bg` | `rgba(0,0,0,0.8)` | Glass panels on 3D canvas |
| `--color-overlay-border` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.2)` | |
| `--shadow-sm/md/lg/xl/overlay` | CSS box-shadow strings | |

`-static` variants exist for `--background`, `--foreground`, `--color-secondary*` — use them where
dark-mode overrides must not apply.

### How to Use Colors by Context

**Tailwind (React components):**
```tsx
// CSS vars are bridged into Tailwind via @theme inline in globals.css
<button className="bg-primary text-white hover:bg-primary-hover" />
// ❌ never: style={{ backgroundColor: '#2F2FE4' }}
```

**Three.js numeric hex:**
```typescript
import { getCssColorHex } from '@/utils/utils'
// Call at render time, NOT at module load
mesh.material.color.set(getCssColorHex('--color-receiver'))
// ❌ never: mesh.material.color.set(0xf0a938)
```

**Canvas 2D:**
```typescript
const color = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement)
  .getPropertyValue('--color-primary').trim()
ctx.fillStyle = color
```

**Speckle FilteringExtension** — resolved hex only (Three.js cannot parse `var(--color-*)`):
```typescript
const hex = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue('--color-warning').trim()
filteringExtension.setUserObjectColors([{ objectIds, color: hex }])
```

**Acoustic material gradient:**
```typescript
import { getMaterialColorByAbsorption } from '@/utils/utils'
const hex = getMaterialColorByAbsorption(0.4)   // → '#hex' between start, mid, end
```

### Rules

1. No alias CSS vars — never `--foo: var(--bar)`.
2. No color constants in `constants.ts` — never `const MY_COLOR = 'var(--color-primary)'`.
3. New colors: reuse the closest existing token. Only add to `globals.css` if truly unique.

### Allowed Color-Adjacent Fields in constants.ts

- `UI_SHADOWS.*` → `"var(--shadow-*)"` strings ✓
- `UI_OVERLAY.BACKDROP_BLUR`, `BORDER_RADIUS` ✓
- Three.js scene constants (`SCENE_GRID`, `SCENE_FOG`) — **no color fields**; call `getCssColorHex` inline ✓

